---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CaptureForm from "../../components/forms/capture-form.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="usignpdf vs DocuSign | E-Signature Alternative"
  seo={{
    page_description: "Why small businesses are switching from DocuSign to usignpdf. Compare pricing, features, and friction.",
    canonical_url: "https://usignpdf.com/compare/docusign/"
  }}
>
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto py-20 px-4 md:px-8">
    <a href="/compare" class="text-accent no-underline hover:underline">&larr; Back to Comparisons</a>
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">usignpdf vs DocuSign</h1>
    <p class="text-xl text-text-muted mb-12">The 800lb gorilla vs the tool that just works.</p>

    <div class="overflow-x-auto mb-16">
        <table class="w-full text-left border-collapse bg-surface rounded-lg overflow-hidden shadow-sm border border-border">
          <thead>
            <tr class="bg-surface-alt">
              <th class="p-4 font-semibold border-b border-border w-1/3">Feature</th>
              <th class="p-4 font-semibold border-b border-border w-1/3 text-primary">DocuSign</th>
              <th class="p-4 font-semibold border-b border-border w-1/3 bg-primary text-surface">usignpdf</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border font-medium">Starting Price</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border">$10-$30/month</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border font-bold text-accent">Free tier available</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border font-medium">Target Audience</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border">Enterprise, Real Estate Brokers</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border font-bold">Freelancers, Solopreneurs</td>
            </tr>
            <tr>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border font-medium">Legally Binding</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border text-success">Yes</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border text-success font-bold">Yes (ESIGN/eIDAS compliant)</td>
            </tr>
             <tr>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border font-medium">Client Account Required?</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border">Often prompts account creation</td>
              <td class="p-4 border-b border-border text-success font-bold">Never</td>
            </tr>
          </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>

    <div class="prose max-w-none mb-12">
        <h2>Why we built an alternative</h2>
        <p>DocuSign is a powerful tool. If you need complex multi-party routing, integration with Salesforce, and conditional logic forms, you should absolutely use them.</p>
        <p>But if you just need to send a PDF to a client and get their signature on it, DocuSign feels like flying a 747 to go to the grocery store. It's expensive, complex, and overkill. We built usignpdf to remove the friction.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="bg-surface-alt p-8 rounded-lg border border-border text-center">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-4">Ready to stop paying enterprise fees?</h3>
        <CaptureForm form="reference" submitLabel="Start Signing Free" />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
